# TextFSM template: Arista EOS `show ip|ipv6 bgp <prefix|community|...>
# [detail]` output. Shared by bgp.route / bgp.community /
# bgp.largecommunity / bgp.aspath because all four commands emit
# the same structural per-path block — though EOS rejects the
# `detail` modifier on the prefix and `regexp` forms when a VRF
# is in play (see pkg/routers/arista_eos.yml header for the
# grammar discussion). The non-detail form is structurally a
# strict subset of the detail form for our purposes, so one
# template covers both.
#
# Canonical block — MODERN EOS (without/with `detail`, recent
# feature releases):
#   BGP routing table entry for 43.157.192.0/18
#    Paths: 1 available
#     3399 5511 7713 132203
#       195.128.254.232 from 195.128.254.232 (195.128.255.252)
#         Origin IGP, metric 0, localpref 100, IGP metric 0, weight 0, tag 0
#         Received 2d19h ago, valid, external, best
#         Community: 1:2 62:2 852:62
#         Extended Community: Link-Bandwidth-AS:3399:12.5 Bps
#         Large Community: 214503:1:2 214503:2:2
#         Rx SAFI: Unicast
#
# Canonical block — LEGACY EOS (older feature releases, kept for
# back-compat and exercised by the textfsm_test fixture):
#   BGP routing table entry for 1.1.1.0/24
#    Paths: (2 available, best #1)
#    Advertised to peers:
#     10.0.0.2
#     65001 65002
#       fe80::1 from fe80::1 (10.0.0.2)
#         Origin IGP, metric 0, localpref 100, weight 0, valid, external, best
#         Community: 65000:100 65000:200
#         Large Community: 214503:8:3607
#         Last update: 1d02h ago
#
# The two shapes differ in three places:
#
#   1. The `Origin` line in MODERN EOS gains trailing fields
#      (`IGP metric N, weight N, tag N`) and DROPS the flag tokens
#      (`valid, external, best`). The flag tokens — including
#      `best` — moved onto a new `Received <age> ago, …, best`
#      line. LEGACY EOS keeps everything on the Origin line and
#      uses `Last update: <age> ago` for the age.
#
#   2. MODERN EOS inserts an `Extended Community: …` line between
#      `Community:` and `Large Community:`. We skip it benignly
#      (no Values captured) so it doesn't disturb FSM anchoring.
#
#   3. MODERN EOS terminates each path block with `Rx SAFI: …`
#      rather than `Last update:`. We trigger `Record` on EITHER
#      terminator, so both shapes flush correctly.
#
# Notes on capture strategy:
#   - `best` is captured either from the LEGACY Origin tail or
#     from the MODERN `Received … ago, …, best` line — whichever
#     appears wins. Both rules use the same `${best}` Value, so
#     the projector sees a single boolean.
#   - `age` is captured either from MODERN `Received <age> ago`
#     or LEGACY `Last update: <age> ago`. Same Value, last write
#     wins per record (only one fires per block).
#   - Both `as_path` and `communities` / `large_communities` are
#     captured as a single token-string (the full whitespace-
#     separated list) rather than via `Value List`. The projector's
#     splitListToken() expands them into per-entry lists when
#     building the wire payload. This sidesteps the gotextfsm
#     gotcha that `${var}(?:\s+${var})*` over `Value List var`
#     only retains the last whitespace-separated occurrence.
#   - `origin (\w+)` excludes the trailing comma so the wire field
#     stays `igp` / `egp` / `incomplete` rather than `igp,`.
#   - The Origin-line tail is matched via an explicit two-branch
#     alternation: the first branch greedy-anchors on a literal
#     `best` keyword (LEGACY); the second branch consumes any
#     trailing comma-separated tokens without capturing `best`
#     (MODERN). The plain `(?:,.*?${best})?\s*$$` pattern WOULD
#     match LEGACY cleanly but reject MODERN (the trailing
#     `IGP metric…, tag 0` after `localpref` leaves non-whitespace
#     between the empty optional group and `\s*$$`).
#   - When the prefix is a BGP aggregate, EOS appends an
#     `(aggregated by <ASN> <router-id>)` suffix to the bare-ASN
#     line, e.g. `13335 (aggregated by 13335 10.34.48.128)`. The
#     bare-ASN pattern below tolerates this suffix via an optional
#     non-capturing trailing group — `${as_path}` itself stays a
#     strict digits-only token so the projector keeps producing a
#     clean integer list. The aggregator ASN / router-id are
#     deliberately not surfaced (no wire field for them on
#     BGPPath today).
Value Filldown prefix ([0-9a-fA-F:.]+/\d+)
Value as_path (\d+(?:\s+\d+)*)
Value nexthop ([0-9a-fA-F:.]+)
Value peer_ip ([0-9a-fA-F:.]+)
Value origin (\w+)
Value med (\d+)
Value local_pref (\d+)
Value communities (\d+:\d+(?:\s+\d+:\d+)*)
Value large_communities (\d+:\d+:\d+(?:\s+\d+:\d+:\d+)*)
Value best (best)
Value age (\S+)

Start
  ^\s*BGP routing table entry for\s+${prefix}
  # Indented bare-ASN line preceding the nexthop block. The
  # optional `(aggregated by <ASN> <router-id>)` trailer is the
  # EOS marker for an aggregate prefix; matched but not captured.
  ^\s+(?P<_as>${as_path})(?:\s+\(aggregated\s+by\s+\d+\s+\S+\))?\s*$$
  # Nexthop line: "<nexthop> [(metric N)] from <peer> (<router-id>)".
  ^\s+${nexthop}\s+(?:\(metric\s+\d+\)\s+)?from\s+${peer_ip}\s+\(\S+\)
  # Origin / metric / localpref — followed by either:
  #   * LEGACY: ", weight N, valid, external, best" (captures best)
  #   * MODERN: ", IGP metric N, weight N, tag N" (no flag tokens)
  # The two-branch alternation accepts either tail; only the
  # LEGACY branch captures `best`. The MODERN flag tokens
  # (`valid`, `external`, `best`) live on the `Received …` line
  # below.
  ^\s+Origin\s+${origin}(?:,\s+metric\s+${med})?(?:,\s+localpref\s+${local_pref})?(?:,[^\n]*?\b${best}\b[^\n]*|,[^\n]*)?\s*$$
  # MODERN: "Received <age> ago, …, best". Captures age (and
  # `best` when present among the comma-separated flag tokens).
  # Does NOT Record — Community / Large Community still follow.
  ^\s+Received\s+${age}\s+ago(?:,[^\n]*?\b${best}\b[^\n]*|,[^\n]*)?\s*$$
  ^\s+Community:\s+${communities}\s*$$
  # MODERN inserts an Extended Community: line between Community:
  # and Large Community:. Skip benignly so it doesn't disturb the
  # FSM (no Values captured — we don't surface extcomms today).
  ^\s+Extended Community:.*$$
  ^\s+Large Community:\s+${large_communities}\s*$$
  # MODERN block terminator: "Rx SAFI: <safi>". Record.
  ^\s+Rx SAFI:.*$$ -> Record
  # LEGACY block terminator: "Last update: <age> ago". Record.
  ^\s+Last update:\s+${age}\s+ago -> Record
  ^\s*$$
